Sure!  In C programming, a loop is used to repeat a block of code multiple times.  There are two types of loops: for and while.  
Here’s an example of a for loop that prints the numbers 1 through 5:

for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    cout << i;
}

and here’s an example of a while loop that prints the numbers 1 through 5:

int i = 1;
while (i <= 5) {
    cout << i;
    i++;
}

